---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import JsonLd from '../../components/JsonLd.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const works = await getCollection('works');
const pl = works.find(w => w.id.endsWith('promised-land.md'));
const { data } = pl!;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const imageLookup = new Map();
data.images?.forEach(img => imageLookup.set(img.src.split('/').pop(), img));
const imageAlt = (filename: string, fallback: string) => imageLookup.get(filename)?.altText || fallback;
---

<Layout title="前往应许之地 — Works" description={data.subtitle}>
  <JsonLd slot="head" data={data} />
  <main class="reader">
    <a href={`${base}/works`} class="reader-back">&larr; Works</a>

    <!-- Opening -->
    <section class="reader-opening">
      <p class="reader-series-name">Toward the Promised Land</p>
      <h1 class="reader-title">前往应许之地</h1>
      <p class="reader-core">
        所有向外的探索，都是向内的寻找。<br />
        所有极致的远行，都是为了回家。
      </p>
      <div class="reader-opening-img">
        <img src={`${base}/images/works/promised-land/odyssey-at-apogee.jpg`} alt={data.coverAltText || data.title} loading="eager" decoding="async" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- About -->
    <section class="reader-notes">
      <h2 class="notes-heading">About</h2>
      <div class="notes-list">
        <span>Odyssey 奥德赛</span>
        <span>Exodus 出埃及记</span>
        <span>Space Exploration 太空探索</span>
        <span>Myth &amp; Faith 神话与信仰</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Exhibition Preface -->
    <section class="reader-preface">
      <h2 class="preface-heading">展览前言</h2>

      <div class="reader-preface-cn">
        <p>在人类历史的长河中，&ldquo;远行&rdquo;从来不只是地理意义上的移动。它更像是一种反复出现的结构：离开、漂泊、失落、召唤，以及归返。</p>
        <p>从古希腊史诗中奥德修斯的漫长归途，到《圣经》中摩西带领族人穿越旷野，人类始终在两种力量之间摆动&mdash;一种是对未知的渴望，一种是对起源的执念。</p>
        <p>而当这种古老的叙事，被投射到宇宙的尺度之上，&ldquo;远方&rdquo;第一次真正成为物理意义上的深空，&ldquo;应许之地&rdquo;，也从神话与信仰，转译为一个尚未抵达的坐标。</p>
        <p>在《前往应许之地》系列中，艺术家将太空探索这一现代命题，与人类最古老的精神原型并置：史诗、宗教、迁徙与流放。火箭、舱室与星历轨道，不再只是技术的象征，而成为一套新的神话装置&mdash;承载着与古代同样的问题：我们为何出发？我们将去往何处？而我们是否仍记得归路？</p>
        <p>人类的探索，从来不是单向的扩张，而是一种环形的运动。我们走得越远，越需要回答一个更古老的问题：我们从哪里来，又要回到哪里去。</p>
        <p>也许，所有的星际航行，本质上都是一次奥德赛。而所谓&ldquo;应许之地&rdquo;，并不在宇宙的彼端，而在那条被拉得无限漫长、却始终未曾断裂的&mdash;归途之上。</p>
      </div>

      <div class="reader-preface-en">
        <p>Throughout the long arc of human history, &ldquo;departure&rdquo; has never been merely a movement through space. It is a recurring structure: leaving, wandering, losing, being called, and returning.</p>
        <p>From the long homeward journey of Odysseus in ancient Greek epic, to Moses leading his people across the wilderness in the Bible, humanity has always oscillated between two forces&mdash;a longing for the unknown, and an attachment to origin.</p>
        <p>When this ancient narrative is projected onto the scale of the cosmos, &ldquo;distance&rdquo; becomes, for the first time, the physical reality of deep space, and the &ldquo;Promised Land&rdquo; is translated from myth and faith into a set of coordinates not yet reached.</p>
        <p>In Toward the Promised Land, the artist juxtaposes the modern project of space exploration with humanity&rsquo;s oldest archetypes: epic, religion, migration, and exile. Rockets, cabins, and orbital trajectories no longer function merely as symbols of technology, but as components of a new myth-making apparatus&mdash;one that carries forward the same enduring questions: Why do we depart? Where are we going? And do we still remember the way home?</p>
        <p>Human exploration has never been a linear expansion, but a circular motion. The farther we travel, the more urgently we are compelled to ask an older question: Where do we come from, and where do we return?</p>
        <p>Perhaps every journey into the stars is, in essence, an odyssey. And the so-called &ldquo;Promised Land&rdquo; does not lie at the far edge of the universe, but along a path stretched to infinity&mdash;a path that has never truly been severed: the way home.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="reader-rule"></div>

    <!-- Work 1: 远地点上的奥德赛 -->
    <section class="reader-work">
      <div class="work-image">
        <img src={`${base}/images/works/promised-land/odyssey-at-apogee.jpg`} alt={imageAlt('odyssey-at-apogee.jpg', '远地点上的奥德赛 Odyssey at Apogee')} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <p class="work-title">远地点上的奥德赛 <span class="work-title-en">Odyssey at Apogee</span></p>
      <p class="work-meta">2020, 布面油画, 100 &times; 70 cm</p>
      <div class="work-text">
        <p>星途漫漫，如史诗里的漂泊。我们向宇宙出发，抵达最远的远地点，才看清回家的方向。在星历表的轨迹之上，续写一场文明的奥德赛。</p>
        <p>远地点，是轨道上离原点最遥远的位置。我们驶向星际尽头，仿佛站在文明与故土最疏离的边缘。正如奥德修斯漂泊越久，归心越炽；人类飞得越远，越要回望来路。</p>
        <p>舷窗外是未知深空，舱内的古希腊戏剧面具，是整个古代文明，凝练成的沉默面孔。飞向远地点，不是为了逃离，而是在最远之处，重新确认起点。</p>
        <p>这场星海远征，看似奔赴未知，实则是漫长的归航。所有向外的探索，都是向内的寻找；所有极致的远行，都是为了回家。</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Work 2: 信徒与流放者 -->
    <section class="reader-work">
      <div class="work-image">
        <img src={`${base}/images/works/promised-land/believers-and-exiles.jpg`} alt={imageAlt('believers-and-exiles.jpg', '信徒与流放者 Believers and Exiles')} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <p class="work-title">信徒与流放者 <span class="work-title-en">Believers and Exiles</span></p>
      <p class="work-meta">2020, 布面油画, 80 &times; 60 cm</p>
      <div class="work-text">
        <p>守夜人在舱内低吟，远行者在星野闯荡。这是文明最古老的叙事：有人守着根脉，有人奔赴旷野，而歌声，是连接彼此的脐带。</p>
        <p>深蓝舱室里，三位女性是文明的守夜人。她们以中古世纪歌者的姿态，用极简的节奏低吟&mdash;唱英雄的残章，唱历史的余响，唱儿女情长，也唱对未知的缄默。这是母亲与子嗣的抚慰，是故土对游子的温柔锚定。</p>
        <p>舱外的漂浮者，是文明的远行者。他在荒芜的星野里闯荡，如同先民踏入原始丛林，带着对未知的渴望，也带着身后吟唱的回响。</p>
        <p>太空并非新的荒野，它只是远古文明的另一种延续&mdash;有人留守，有人远行；有人低吟，有人闯荡。而所有的流放，终会被这低吟，牵回文明的母腹。</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Work 3: 应许之地的太空羊 -->
    <section class="reader-work">
      <div class="work-image">
        <img src={`${base}/images/works/promised-land/space-sheep-of-the-promised-land.jpg`} alt={imageAlt('space-sheep-of-the-promised-land.jpg', '应许之地的太空羊 Space Sheep of the Promised Land')} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <p class="work-title">应许之地的太空羊 <span class="work-title-en">Space Sheep of the Promised Land</span></p>
      <p class="work-meta">2020, 布面油画, 70 &times; 70 cm</p>
      <div class="work-text">
        <p>一如摩西引领族人穿越旷野，众生亦如羔羊，被历史驱向宇宙的新境。这是新神的应许之地，也是未知的荒漠。多数个体，不过在宏大叙事之中，谋求一隅微小的立足之地。</p>
        <p>废土的车辆载着羊群驶向终点，火箭仍在不断运来新的抵达者。他们是奔赴星海的先驱，亦是被投向深空的，沉默的羔羊。</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="reader-end"></div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .reader {
    max-width: 880px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: calc(var(--spacing-xl) + 2rem) var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-xl);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
  }

  .reader-back {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }

  /* Opening */
  .reader-opening {
    margin-bottom: calc(var(--spacing-xl) + 2rem);
  }

  .reader-series-name {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }

  .reader-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    font-weight: 300;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .reader-core {
    max-width: 680px;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .reader-opening-img {
    margin: var(--spacing-md) calc(-1 * var(--spacing-md)) 0;
  }

  .reader-opening-img img {
    width: 100%;
    display: block;
    background: #eaeaea;
  }

  /* About notes */
  .reader-notes {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto calc(var(--spacing-xl) + 2rem);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: var(--spacing-xs) 0 var(--spacing-xs) var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .notes-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .notes-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }

  .notes-list span {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  /* Preface */
  .reader-preface {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .preface-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .reader-preface-cn {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.95;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .reader-preface-cn p {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    text-indent: 2em;
  }

  .reader-preface-cn p:first-child {
    text-indent: 0;
  }

  .reader-preface-en {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .reader-preface-en p {
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  }

  /* Works */
  .reader-work {
    margin-bottom: calc(var(--spacing-xl) + 2rem);
  }

  .reader-work:last-of-type {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .work-image {
    margin: 0 calc(-1 * var(--spacing-md)) var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .work-image img {
    width: 100%;
    display: block;
    background: #eaeaea;
  }

  .work-title {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .work-title-en {
    font-weight: 300;
    opacity: 0.45;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .work-meta {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto var(--spacing-md);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .work-text {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .work-text p {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    text-indent: 2em;
  }

  .work-text p:first-child {
    text-indent: 0;
  }

  /* Dividers */
  .reader-rule {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: var(--spacing-lg) auto;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--color-border);
    opacity: 0.4;
  }

  .reader-end {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: calc(var(--spacing-xl) + 2rem) auto 0;
    text-align: center;
    padding-top: var(--spacing-xl);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  /* Mobile */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .reader {
      padding: calc(var(--spacing-lg) + 3rem) var(--spacing-sm) var(--spacing-lg);
    }

    .reader-opening {
      margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
    }

    .reader-title {
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 2.75rem);
    }

    .reader-opening-img,
    .work-image {
      margin-left: calc(-1 * var(--spacing-sm));
      margin-right: calc(-1 * var(--spacing-sm));
    }

    .reader-preface,
    .reader-notes,
    .work-text,
    .reader-rule,
    .work-title,
    .work-meta {
      max-width: 100%;
    }

    .reader-notes {
      padding-left: var(--spacing-md);
    }

    .work-title {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .work-text,
    .reader-preface-cn {
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
    }
  }
</style>
